    "demo": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <title>Modal dialog demo</title>\n    <style>\n      :root {\n        color-scheme: light dark;\n        --bg: #ffffff;\n        --fg: #1a1a1a;\n        --muted: #4a4a4a;\n        --accent: #0b57d0;\n        --danger: #b3261e;\n        --surface: #f3f4f6;\n      }\n      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n        :root {\n          --bg: #121212;\n          --fg: #f0f0f0;\n          --muted: #c4c4c4;\n          --accent: #8ab4f8;\n          --danger: #f2b8b5;\n          --surface: #1f1f1f;\n        }\n      }\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 2rem 1rem;\n        font:\n          1rem/1.5 system-ui,\n          sans-serif;\n        background: var(--bg);\n        color: var(--fg);\n      }\n      main {\n        max-width: 40rem;\n        margin: 0 auto;\n      }\n      button {\n        font: inherit;\n        padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\n        border: 2px solid var(--fg);\n        border-radius: 0.375rem;\n        background: var(--bg);\n        color: var(--fg);\n        cursor: pointer;\n      }\n      button.danger {\n        border-color: var(--danger);\n        color: var(--danger);\n      }\n      :focus-visible {\n        outline: 3px solid var(--accent);\n        outline-offset: 2px;\n      }\n      dialog {\n        max-width: min(32rem, calc(100vw - 2rem));\n        border: 2px solid var(--fg);\n        border-radius: 0.5rem;\n        background: var(--bg);\n        color: var(--fg);\n        padding: 1.5rem;\n      }\n      dialog::backdrop {\n        background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6);\n      }\n      .actions {\n        display: flex;\n        gap: 0.75rem;\n        justify-content: flex-end;\n        flex-wrap: wrap;\n      }\n      body.locked {\n        overflow: hidden;\n      }\n      p.muted {\n        color: var(--muted);\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <main>\n      <h1>Project settings</h1>\n      <p>Deleting a project removes its files for everyone on the team.</p>\n      <p>\n        <button type=\"button\" id=\"open-delete\" class=\"danger\">\n          Delete project\n        </button>\n      </p>\n      <p class=\"muted\" id=\"result\" role=\"status\"></p>\n      <p><a href=\"#top\">Back to top</a></p>\n    </main>\n\n    <dialog\n      id=\"delete-dialog\"\n      aria-labelledby=\"delete-title\"\n      aria-describedby=\"delete-desc\"\n    >\n      <h2 id=\"delete-title\">Delete this project?</h2>\n      <p id=\"delete-desc\">\n        The project and its 12 files are removed. This cannot be undone.\n      </p>\n      <form method=\"dialog\" class=\"actions\">\n        <button value=\"cancel\" autofocus>Cancel</button>\n        <button value=\"delete\" class=\"danger\">Delete</button>\n      </form>\n    </dialog>\n\n    <script>\n      const opener = document.getElementById(\"open-delete\");\n      const dialog = document.getElementById(\"delete-dialog\");\n      const result = document.getElementById(\"result\");\n\n      opener.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n        document.body.classList.add(\"locked\");\n        dialog.showModal();\n      });\n\n      dialog.addEventListener(\"close\", () => {\n        document.body.classList.remove(\"locked\");\n        result.textContent =\n          dialog.returnValue === \"delete\"\n            ? \"Project deleted.\"\n            : \"Nothing was deleted.\";\n        opener.focus();\n      });\n\n      dialog.addEventListener(\"click\", (event) => {\n        if (event.target === dialog) dialog.close(\"cancel\");\n      });\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n",
    "description": "Build an accessible modal dialog or popup with focus trap, Escape to close and focus return",
    "expectations": "# Expectations: dialog-modal\n\n1. Activating the opener button shows an element with role `dialog` whose accessible name equals the dialog's visible heading text.\n2. After opening, `document.activeElement` is inside the dialog.\n3. While the dialog is open, pressing Tab 10 times never moves focus to a page element outside the dialog (focus leaving the document for browser chrome, seen as `document.body`, is allowed).\n4. While the dialog is open, every element outside it is inert or hidden from the accessibility tree: an element behind the dialog cannot be focused with `.focus()`.\n5. Pressing Escape closes the dialog (it is no longer in the accessibility tree) and focus returns to the opener.\n6. Activating the dialog's cancel or close button closes it and focus returns to the opener.\n",
