    "demo": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <title>Redundant entry demo</title>\n    <style>\n      :root {\n        color-scheme: light dark;\n        --bg: #ffffff;\n        --fg: #1a1a1a;\n        --accent: #0b57d0;\n      }\n      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n        :root {\n          --bg: #121212;\n          --fg: #f0f0f0;\n          --accent: #8ab4f8;\n        }\n      }\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 2rem 1rem;\n        font:\n          1rem/1.5 system-ui,\n          sans-serif;\n        background: var(--bg);\n        color: var(--fg);\n      }\n      main {\n        max-width: 32rem;\n        margin: 0 auto;\n      }\n      .field {\n        margin-bottom: 1rem;\n      }\n      label {\n        display: block;\n        font-weight: 600;\n      }\n      .check {\n        font-weight: 400;\n      }\n      input:not([type=\"checkbox\"]) {\n        box-sizing: border-box;\n        width: 100%;\n        padding: 0.5rem;\n        font: inherit;\n      }\n      fieldset {\n        margin: 0 0 1rem;\n        border: 1px solid currentColor;\n      }\n      button {\n        padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\n        font: inherit;\n      }\n      :focus-visible {\n        outline: 3px solid var(--accent);\n        outline-offset: 2px;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <main>\n      <h1>Checkout</h1>\n      <form>\n        <h2>Delivery address</h2>\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"street\">Street and number</label>\n          <input\n            id=\"street\"\n            name=\"street\"\n            autocomplete=\"shipping address-line1\"\n          />\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"city\">City</label>\n          <input id=\"city\" name=\"city\" autocomplete=\"shipping address-level2\" />\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"postal\">Postal code</label>\n          <input\n            id=\"postal\"\n            name=\"postal\"\n            autocomplete=\"shipping postal-code\"\n          />\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"country\">Country</label>\n          <input\n            id=\"country\"\n            name=\"country\"\n            autocomplete=\"shipping country-name\"\n          />\n        </div>\n        <fieldset>\n          <legend>Billing address</legend>\n          <label class=\"check\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"same\" checked />\n            Same as delivery address\n          </label>\n          <div id=\"billing\" hidden>\n            <div class=\"field\">\n              <label for=\"billing-street\">Street and number</label>\n              <input\n                id=\"billing-street\"\n                name=\"billing-street\"\n                autocomplete=\"billing address-line1\"\n              />\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"field\">\n              <label for=\"billing-city\">City</label>\n              <input\n                id=\"billing-city\"\n                name=\"billing-city\"\n                autocomplete=\"billing address-level2\"\n              />\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"field\">\n              <label for=\"billing-postal\">Postal code</label>\n              <input\n                id=\"billing-postal\"\n                name=\"billing-postal\"\n                autocomplete=\"billing postal-code\"\n              />\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"field\">\n              <label for=\"billing-country\">Country</label>\n              <input\n                id=\"billing-country\"\n                name=\"billing-country\"\n                autocomplete=\"billing country-name\"\n              />\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </fieldset>\n        <button type=\"submit\">Place order</button>\n      </form>\n    </main>\n    <script>\n      const same = document.getElementById(\"same\");\n      const billing = document.getElementById(\"billing\");\n\n      same.addEventListener(\"change\", () => {\n        billing.hidden = same.checked;\n      });\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n",
    "description": "Never make people type the same details twice in one process; prefill or offer \"same as delivery address\" for billing, invoice and later steps",
    "expectations": "# Expectations: redundant-entry\n\n1. After the earlier fields are filled in, the later fields that ask for the same information hold the same values, are hidden behind a checked \"same as\" choice, or are filled by one control the user activates.\n2. The later fields can still take different values: after the reuse, turning the choice off (when there is one) leaves every later field visible and editable.\n",
