    "demo": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <title>Sign-in without puzzles demo</title>\n    <style>\n      :root {\n        color-scheme: light dark;\n        --bg: #ffffff;\n        --fg: #1a1a1a;\n        --accent: #0b57d0;\n      }\n      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n        :root {\n          --bg: #121212;\n          --fg: #f0f0f0;\n          --accent: #8ab4f8;\n        }\n      }\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 2rem 1rem;\n        font:\n          1rem/1.5 system-ui,\n          sans-serif;\n        background: var(--bg);\n        color: var(--fg);\n      }\n      main {\n        max-width: 32rem;\n        margin: 0 auto;\n      }\n      .field {\n        margin-bottom: 1rem;\n      }\n      label {\n        display: block;\n        font-weight: 600;\n      }\n      .check {\n        font-weight: 400;\n      }\n      input:not([type=\"checkbox\"]) {\n        box-sizing: border-box;\n        width: 100%;\n        padding: 0.5rem;\n        font: inherit;\n      }\n      fieldset {\n        margin: 0 0 1rem;\n        border: 1px solid currentColor;\n      }\n      button {\n        padding: 0.5rem 1rem;\n        font: inherit;\n      }\n      :focus-visible {\n        outline: 3px solid var(--accent);\n        outline-offset: 2px;\n      }\n      .trap {\n        position: absolute;\n        left: -10000px;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <main>\n      <h1>Sign in</h1>\n      <form id=\"sign-in\">\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"email\">Email</label>\n          <input\n            id=\"email\"\n            name=\"email\"\n            type=\"email\"\n            autocomplete=\"username\"\n            required\n          />\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"password\">Password</label>\n          <input\n            id=\"password\"\n            name=\"password\"\n            type=\"password\"\n            autocomplete=\"current-password\"\n            required\n          />\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"trap\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n          <label for=\"website\">Leave this empty</label>\n          <input id=\"website\" name=\"website\" tabindex=\"-1\" autocomplete=\"off\" />\n        </div>\n        <button type=\"submit\">Sign in</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" id=\"email-link\">Email me a sign-in link</button>\n      </form>\n      <p id=\"result\" role=\"status\"></p>\n    </main>\n    <script>\n      const form = document.getElementById(\"sign-in\");\n      const result = document.getElementById(\"result\");\n\n      form.addEventListener(\"submit\", (event) => {\n        event.preventDefault();\n        if (form.website.value !== \"\" || !form.reportValidity()) return;\n        form.hidden = true;\n        result.textContent = \"Welcome back, you are signed in.\";\n      });\n\n      document.getElementById(\"email-link\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n        result.textContent = \"Check your email for a sign-in link.\";\n      });\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n",
    "description": "Sign-in, login, CAPTCHA and bot checks. No typing distorted letters, solving puzzles or remembering codes to get in; allow paste and password managers",
    "expectations": "# Expectations: sign-in-without-puzzles\n\n1. Signing in needs no puzzle: with only the email and password filled in, signing in succeeds; or a single action that tests nothing (an \"I am human\" checkbox) or a control that does the check for the user (such as \"Fill letters for me\") lets signing in succeed; or the form offers another way in (such as an emailed sign-in link) that needs no puzzle.\n2. The password field carries `autocomplete=\"current-password\"`, the email field `username` or `email`, and pasting into the password field works.\n",
