    "demo": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <title>Shop - Acme</title>\n    <style>\n      :root {\n        color-scheme: light dark;\n        --bg: #ffffff;\n        --fg: #1a1a1a;\n        --band: #f3f4f6;\n        --accent: #0b57d0;\n      }\n      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n        :root {\n          --bg: #121212;\n          --fg: #f0f0f0;\n          --band: #1f1f1f;\n          --accent: #8ab4f8;\n        }\n      }\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        font:\n          1rem/1.5 system-ui,\n          sans-serif;\n        background: var(--bg);\n        color: var(--fg);\n      }\n      a {\n        color: var(--accent);\n      }\n      :focus-visible {\n        outline: 3px solid var(--accent);\n        outline-offset: 2px;\n      }\n      h1:focus {\n        outline: none;\n      }\n      header {\n        background: var(--band);\n        padding: 1rem;\n      }\n      nav ul {\n        display: flex;\n        flex-wrap: wrap;\n        gap: 1rem;\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 0;\n        list-style: none;\n      }\n      [aria-current=\"page\"] {\n        font-weight: 700;\n        text-decoration-thickness: 3px;\n      }\n      main {\n        max-width: 48rem;\n        margin: 0 auto;\n        padding: 2rem 1rem;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <header>\n      <nav aria-label=\"Main\">\n        <ul role=\"list\">\n          <li><a href=\"?view=shop\" data-route aria-current=\"page\">Shop</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"?view=journal\" data-route>Journal</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"?view=about\" data-route>About</a></li>\n        </ul>\n      </nav>\n    </header>\n    <main id=\"outlet\"></main>\n    <script>\n      const views = {\n        shop: {\n          title: \"Shop\",\n          html: '<h1>Shop</h1><p>New arrivals for the autumn season.</p><p><a href=\"#rain-jacket\">Rain jacket</a></p>',\n        },\n        journal: {\n          title: \"Journal\",\n          html: '<h1>Journal</h1><p>Stories from the trail.</p><p><a href=\"#first-post\">Crossing the Tatras in October</a></p>',\n        },\n        about: {\n          title: \"About\",\n          html: '<h1>About</h1><p>Acme makes outdoor gear in Brno.</p><p><a href=\"#contact\">Contact us</a></p>',\n        },\n      };\n      const outlet = document.getElementById(\"outlet\");\n      const nav = document.querySelector(\"nav\");\n      const viewOf = (url) =>\n        new URL(url, location.href).searchParams.get(\"view\") ?? \"shop\";\n\n      function render(url, { focus }) {\n        const key = viewOf(url);\n        const view = views[key] ?? {\n          title: \"Page not found\",\n          html: \"<h1>Page not found</h1><p>Use the navigation to continue.</p>\",\n        };\n        outlet.innerHTML = view.html;\n        document.title = view.title + \" - Acme\";\n        for (const link of nav.querySelectorAll(\"a\")) {\n          if (viewOf(link.href) === key)\n            link.setAttribute(\"aria-current\", \"page\");\n          else link.removeAttribute(\"aria-current\");\n        }\n        if (focus) {\n          const heading = outlet.querySelector(\"h1\");\n          heading.tabIndex = -1;\n          heading.focus();\n          window.scrollTo(0, 0);\n        }\n      }\n      document.addEventListener(\"click\", (event) => {\n        const link = event.target.closest(\"a[data-route]\");\n        if (\n          !link ||\n          event.metaKey ||\n          event.ctrlKey ||\n          event.shiftKey ||\n          event.button !== 0\n        )\n          return;\n        event.preventDefault();\n        history.pushState({}, \"\", link.href);\n        render(link.href, { focus: true });\n      });\n      window.addEventListener(\"popstate\", () =>\n        render(location.href, { focus: true })\n      );\n      render(location.href, { focus: false });\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n",
    "description": "Manage focus, page title and announcements on client-side route changes in a React, Vue or SPA router",
    "expectations": "# Expectations: spa-route-change\n\n1. Activating an in-app navigation link with the keyboard changes `document.title` to a value that contains the new view's `h1` text.\n2. After the route change, `document.activeElement` is the new view's `h1` (or the `main` element), not `body` and not the activated link.\n3. After the route change, the next Tab press focuses an element inside `main`.\n4. The navigation link for the current view has `aria-current=\"page\"` and no other navigation link has it.\n5. Pressing the browser Back button restores the previous view and its `document.title`.\n6. On initial page load, focus is not moved by script (`document.activeElement` is `body`).\n",
